hadiths[69]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7003","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Warqa bin Omar told us, about Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Ali to Yemen and said: “Teach them the laws And judge between them.” He said: “I have no knowledge of judgment.” So he pushed him in the chest and said: “O God, guide him to justice.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7003 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7004","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told us, Amer bin Ibrahim Al-Anbari told us, Faraj bin Fadala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that two men disputed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he said to Amr: “Judge between them.” He said: “Judge between them while you are present, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Yes, for if you are correct, you will have ten rewards, and if you strive hard and make a mistake, you will have a reward.” This hadith has an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it. In this context """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7004 - Faraj bin Fadalah weak"
"7005","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya told me, Abu Omar al-Hudhi told me, Hammam told me, on the authority of Qatada, he told me Al-Ala’ bin Ziyad, and Yazid, Mutarrif’s brother, told me, and two other men, whose names Hammam has forgotten, told me that Mutarrif told them that Iyad bin Hammad told him that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say in his sermon: “The companions of Paradise are three: one with established authority and one who is just and successful.” And a merciful and tender-hearted man to all his relatives, and a poor and chaste man. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7005 - Narrated by Muslim"
"7006","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdul-A’la told us, Muammar, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The “Those who are just in this world will be on podiums of pearls on the Day of Resurrection before the Most Gracious, the Mighty and Majestic, because of what they have done justly in this world.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs, and they have all included it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7006 - They brought it out"
"7007","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq, the jurist, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Atban ibn Malik informed us, Uyaynah ibn Abd informed us. The Most Gracious, Marwan bin Abdullah, the client of Safwan bin Hudhayfah, informed me on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people of injustice and their helpers are in Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7007 - Munkar"
"7008","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Shami told me, saying: Al-Hasan bin Hammad Al-Kufi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Adawi told us, He said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the pulpit, saying: Ubadah bin Abdullah bin Ubadah told me, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaid Allah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O people, God will not accept the prayer of an imam who rules other than what God has revealed.” He mentioned the rest of the hadith: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7008 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"7009","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Makhramah bin Bukair told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Bishr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No one is appointed over ten people.” Then he ascends, not treating them justly, but he will come on the Day of Resurrection in shackles and shackles.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and we do not narrate it. We are excused for leaving out the hadiths of Makhramah bin Bukayr at all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7009 - True"
"7010","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih, may God have mercy on him, told us in Baghdad. Abu Dawud Suleiman bin al-Ash’ath and Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, They said: Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, that people asked Usama bin Zaid, that this man speak to us, meaning Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, said: We spoke to him without him opening a door, lest he be the first to open it. What I say: Your princes. Your choice after something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The ruler who was obeyed in disobeying God Almighty will be brought, and he will be ordered to the Fire and thrown.” Then his hooves - meaning his intestines - will stick out, and he will move around in it as a donkey moves in a mill, and the people who are obedient to him will come upon him. So they say to him: Yes, wherever you are, you are ordering us? He says: I used to order you to do one matter and disagree with you to do something else. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7010 - True"
"7011","Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farwi told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi told us Al-Mawwal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mawhib, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him On her authority, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Six have been cursed by God, cursed by God, and every prophet will be answered: the one who denies God’s decree, and the one who does not In the Book of God, and the one who rules with might to humiliate what God has made honorable and honor what God has humiliated, and the one who makes lawful what God has forbidden, and the one who makes lawful from my family God forbids, and the one who abandons my Sunnah “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7011 - The hadith is completely objectionable"
"7012","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Shihab bin Abbad told us, Abdullah bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Judges are three: two judges in Hell and one judge in Paradise. A judge who knew the truth and ruled according to it will be in Paradise, and a judge who knew the truth and was unjust intentionally will be in Hell, and a judge who ruled without knowledge will be in Hell. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and it has a witness with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7012 - Ibn Bukayr Al-Ghanawi denies the hadith and said that he has an authentic witness."
"7013","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Ghassan told us, and Ali bin Hakim told us. Sharik, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Two judges in Hell and one judge in Paradise. A judge who ruled truthfully will be in Paradise, a judge who ruled unjustly will be in Hell, and a judge who ruled out of ignorance then he will be in Hell. They said: What is his fault? This one who is ignorant said: “It is his fault that he is not a judge until he knows.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7013 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7014","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, about Amer Al-Dahni, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Maqil, on the authority of her father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one is in control of any of the matters Whether this nation is small or large, there is no one who does justice among them except that God will cast him into Hell.” This is Umm Maqil, the daughter of Maqil bin Sinan Al-Ashja’i, and she is The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7014 - True"
"7015","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah, Asim bin Bahdala reported on the authority of Yazid bin Sharik that Al-Dahhak bin Qays sent a piece of clothing with him to Marwan bin Al-Hakam, and he said: Marwan to the doorman: Look who is at the door? He said: Abu Hurairah, so he gave him permission and said: O Abu Hurairah, tell us something that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “A man will soon wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades and had not attained anything from the affairs of the people.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7015 - True"
"7016","Professor Abu Al-Walid and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, Muadh bin Sufyan told us. Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Abi Ali, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Woe to the princes, and woe to the officials, and woe to the trustworthy people, who make people wish on the Day of Resurrection that their tails were hanging from the Pleiades.” “They are directed between the heaven and the earth, and they have not been able to do anything.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7016 - True"
"7017","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah told us Bin Yazid Al-Muqri, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jaafar, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Salem Al-Habashani, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Abu Dharr, I see that you are weak, so do not command two people or “You shall take charge of the property of an orphan.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7017 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7018","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Al-Sammak told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Abi told us Dhi’ib, on the authority of Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “Whoever is appointed a judge, it is as if he had been slaughtered without a knife.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7018 - True"
"7019","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, my father told me, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yazid Al-Hadrami, that Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Command me. He said: “You are weak, and it is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection it will be shame and regret.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. It was said: On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Dharr
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7019 - True"
"7020","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Sadaqa bin Musa told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, On the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, command me. He said: “The emirate is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection it will be shame and regret, except for the one who commanded what was right and fulfilled what was owed to him in it.”"
"7021","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told me, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Bilal bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that Al-Hajjaj wanted to appoint him as judge of Basra, so Anas said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Whoever seeks judgment and seeks help for it, it will be entrusted to him, and whoever does not seek it and does not seek help from him, an angel will be appointed for him.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7021 - True"
"7022","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abd told me Al-Aziz, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubayd Allah, that Suleiman bin Habib told them on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The knots of Islam will be broken, one by one loop. Whenever a loop is broken, it clings to the one that follows it, and the first to break it.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “This Abdul Aziz is Ibn Ubaid Allah bin Hamza bin Suhaib. Ismail is Ibn Ubayd Allah Ibn Al-Muhajir, and the entire chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7023","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yazid bin Abdul Aziz Al-Tayalisi told us, Khalid bin Abdullah Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Hussein bin Qais Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever employs a man from a group, and in that group there is someone more pleasing to God than him, has betrayed God, betrayed His Messenger, and betrayed The believers: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7023 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7024","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Hasan bin Ahmad Al-Harrani told us, Jeddi told us, Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Bakr bin Khunays, on the authority of Raja’ bin Haywa, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Sufyan, who said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said to me, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him when he sent me to the Levant: O Yazid, you are a relative of mine. I hope you will prefer them to the leadership. This is what I fear most for you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is appointed in charge of the affairs of the Muslims and appoints someone over them out of favoritism, the curse of God will be upon him. God will not accept it from him.” pure and without justice until He admits him to Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7025","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan al-Bazzar informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected on Safa. Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd told us. Saeed bin Mansour, told us by Sharik, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me To Yemen, and I said: You are sending me to a people with teeth, and I am young. He said: “When two adversaries sit before you, do not judge for one of them until you hear from the other as you heard from the first.” Ali said: I will still judge “this.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7025 - True"
"7026","Azhar bin Hamdoun the caller told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Abu Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is with the judge as long as he does not do justice.” “So when he commits a crime, God Almighty disavows him.” This Abu Al-Awwam: Imran bin Dawud Al-Qattan, and the chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7026 - True"
"7027","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymrah, on the authority of Abu Maryam, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He says: “Whoever takes charge of any of the affairs of the Muslims and conceals himself without regard to their seclusion, their need, their poverty, or their need, God Almighty and Majestic will conceal Himself on the Day of Resurrection.” “The Resurrection without his seclusion, poverty, need, and poverty.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He did not narrate it, and its chain of narration is authentically Syrian. “And it has a witness.” With an authentic chain of transmission from Al-Basri, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah Al-Juhani, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7027 - True"
"7028","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I said to Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, may God be pleased with him: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever closes his door to those in need, solitude and need, God will close the door of heaven to the exclusion of those in need, solitude and poverty. And its sedation”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7028 - True"
"7029","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Musab bin Thabit bin Abdullah informed me. Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, that his father, Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, had a dispute between him and his brother Amr Ibn Al-Zubayr, so Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr entered Al-Zubair came to Saeed bin Al-Aas, and Amr bin Al-Zubair was with him on the bed, and Saeed said to Abdullah: “Here. He said: No, the decree of the Messenger of God and the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is that the two adversaries sit before the judge. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7029 - True"
"7030","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Whoever is presented with a judgment, let him judge according to what is in the Book of God, and if it comes to him A matter is not in the Book of God Almighty, then let him decide according to what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of God Almighty, and he does not His Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decrees it, so let him judge according to what the righteous have said. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of God and his Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, does not decree it. And the righteous have not decided for it, so let him exert his opinion, but if it is not good, then let him acknowledge it and not be ashamed. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They bring it out: “And the judge is: Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Allah bin Masoud.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7030 - True"
"7031","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abu Musa: “Two men brought a camel or an animal to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And there is no evidence for either of them, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed it between them. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Hammam bin Yahya bin Saeed bin Abi Arouba disagreed with the text of this hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7031 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7032","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Al-Walid told me, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, Al-Hasan told us Ibn Sufyan, Hadba Ibn Khalid told us, Hammam Ibn Yahya told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Moses: “Two men claimed a camel, and each of them produced two witnesses, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided it among them.” And this hadith as well. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7032 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7033","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed me, Usama bin Zaid informed me, about... The freed slave of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: Two men came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, hastening over inheritances between them that were not They have proof. “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to divide and separate each other, then draw shares and let each one of them make lawful to his companion.” The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it. “And Umm Salamah’s client is: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, which is mentioned in the two Sahih books.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7033 - True"
"7034","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, And Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam, they said: Al-Fadl bin Sulaiman told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, the client of Umm Salamah, told me. He said: I heard Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, saying: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and two men came to him, disputing between them about an inheritance, and there was no One of them had evidence, and each of them said to his companion: O Messenger of God, this is what I asked of so-and-so. He said: “No, but go, and be careful, then ask, then divide, then let each one of you make his companion lawful.” This is an authentic hadith, subject to the condition. Muslim and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7034 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7035","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man claimed a right from another man, so they disputed with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him and asked him for proof, so he said: I have no proof. Then he said to the other: Swear. So he swore and said: By God, I have nothing. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, he is with you. Pay him his due.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Your testimony “There is no god but God as an atonement for your oath.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7035 - True"
"7036","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see my nation being afraid, do not say to the oppressor, O oppressor, for you may be saved from them.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7036 - True"
"7037","Ali bin Muhammad bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani told me, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Malik bin Ismail Al-Nahdi told us, Al-Ajlah told us, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Khalil, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, was sent by the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Yemen. Then three people rose up to him, disputing with a son, each one claiming that he was his son. He said: So he left two of them alone and said: “Do you feel comfortable with this one who is left?” They said: No, and he was alone with two of them and he told them the same thing. They said: No, so he said: “I see you as quarreling partners, and I am casting lots among you, so I cast lots among them and assigned it to one of them and fined him two-thirds of the blood money.” For the rest.” He said: “Then he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed until his molars became visible.” The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, reported on the authority of Al-Ajlah bin Abdullah Al-Kindi, and his narrations are not abandoned, for the one against whom vengeance is taken is his doctrine.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7037 - Al-Ajlah is not the one who is abandoned"
"7038","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yusuf, the servant of Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: She was the slave girl of Zamah whom he had sexual intercourse with, and she was thinking of a man. Another is that he had intercourse with her, and Zam’ah died while she was pregnant, and she gave birth to a boy resembling the man he was suspected of. So Sawda mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “As for the inheritance, it is his, but as for you, hide from him, for you have no brother.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7038 - True"
"7039","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ziyad bin Saad told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Osama, that Abu Maimunah Sulayman, from the people of Medina, an honest man, said: While I was sitting With Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, a Persian woman came to him with her son, and her husband had divorced her. She said: O Abu Hurairah. Then she chanted and said in Persian: “My husband wants to take my son away.” Then her husband came and said: “Who will be unfair to me?” Abu Hurairah said: I do not say anything about this except that I heard that a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was with him. She said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. My husband wants to take my son to drink from the well of my father Utbah, and it has benefited me, so he said: “Ask them.” On him.” Her husband said: “Who is unjust to me regarding my son, O Messenger of God?” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, so take it.” In the hand, whichever you wish.” So the boy took his mother’s hand and she started with him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7039 - True"
"7040","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abu Kamil Al-Jahdari told us, Fudayl bin Suleiman, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Yahya, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided And he made peace regarding the palm tree and the two and three palm trees, but they differed regarding the rights of that, so he decreed that every palm tree with the amount of its leaf has a harem. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7040 - True"
"7041","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, it was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “The harem of the heart of the ordinary is fifty cubits. And the harem of Qalib al-Nadi is twenty-five cubits. It was related and transmitted by Umar ibn Qays, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The harem of a regular well is fifty cubits, and the harem of a regular well is twenty-five cubits. an arm"
"7042","Ibrahim bin Ismat Al-Adl told us, Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Muhammad bin Al-Furat Al-Tamimi told us, he said: I heard Muharib bin Dathar said: Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them, told me that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A false witness does not “His feet will move until God brings them to Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7042 - True"
"7043","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Bishr bin Suleiman the Muezzin, Sayyar Abu Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: We were with Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, before the Hour is the handing over of property and the dispersal of trade until the woman helps her husband in trade and severing “The relatives and the appearance of false testimony and the concealment of the testimony of the truth” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7043 - True"
"7044","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muhammad told me Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “There was nothing more hateful to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, of lying, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has tried it from anyone, even if it is small, then it will come out of him until he renews it. “He has repentance.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7044 - True"
"7045","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzani told us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi, Amr bin Malik Al-Basri told us, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Masmoul told us, Abdullah bin Salamah bin Wahram told us, on the authority of Tawus Al-Yamani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: It was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man giving testimony, and he said To me: “O Ibn Abbas, bear witness only to what shines for you like the light of this sun.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gestured with his hand to the sun. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7045 - Wow"
"7046","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf bin Shajarat Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Sufi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Ali, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you, for truth is reassurance and lying is doubt.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7046 - Its chain of transmission is strong"
"7047","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Hisham told us, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayed bin Salam, on the authority of his grandfather Matur, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what Sin? He said: “If something wavers in your heart, leave it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7047 - True"
"7048","Abu Al-Hussein bin Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Balkhi told me, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Maryam, Nafi’ bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Ata’ bin Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The testimony of a Bedouin against the owner of a village is not permissible.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7048 - The author did not authenticate it, and it is an objectionable hadith despite the cleanliness of its chain of transmission."
"7049","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Humaidi told us, Muslim bin told us Khalid, Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to bear witness “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7049 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7050","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abdullah bin Musa told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, regarding the two boys’ testimony, he said: God Almighty said: {Of those among the witnesses whom you are satisfied with?} [Al-Baqarah: 282] He said: “It is not “Boys are among those he pleases.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7050 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7051","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he informed us Abu Hamza, Ibrahim Al-Sayegh told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever helps an opponent unjustly will be in the wrath of God until he is removed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7051 - True"
"7052","Muhammad bin Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Arim Abu al-Nu`man told us, Mu`tamar bin Suleiman, he said: I heard my father, speaking on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Whoever aids falsehood in order to refute With its true falsehood, he has been freed from the protection of God and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7052 - Hanash Al-Rahbi is weak"
"7053","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ja’far al-Mada’ani told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, On the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “The child of fornication is not responsible for any of the burden of his parents” {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another} [Al-An’am: 164] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not They bring it out.” Its opposite has been authenticated with two authentic chain of narrations. As for the first chain of narrations, “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7053 - It is correct and the opposite is correct"
"7054","So Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, Suhail told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the child of adultery. He said: “He is the worst of the three.” As for the chain of transmission The second"
"7055","So Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Amr bin Awn Al-Wasiti told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abu Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The child of adultery is the worst of the three.”"
"7056","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ata’, Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Aws and Khazraj were proud, and the Aws said: Among us is the one whose testimony was approved by the testimony of two men.” Khuzaymah bin Thabit: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7056 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7057","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Masruq, on the authority of Ishaq Ibn Al-Furat, on the authority of Laith Ibn Saad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he greeted the response of the oath to the seeker of the truth. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7057 - I do not know Muhammad and I fear that the hadith is not false."
"7058","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, On the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of al-Walid ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Reconciliation It is permissible among Muslims.” This is witnessed by the hadith of Amr ibn Aoun, and by it it is known.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7058 - Munkar"
"7059","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, many times we told him. Ibn Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Aoun, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Reconciliation is permissible between “The Muslims are bound to their conditions, except for a condition that prohibits what is permissible or makes permissible what is forbidden.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7059 - Wow"
"7060","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Hayyan told us, Ibrahim bin Muawiyah told us Abu Ishaq Al-Karabisi, Hisham bin Yusuf, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, placed a stone on Muadh took his money and sold it for a debt he owed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7060 - True"
"7061","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said that a man was buying at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was weakness in his knot, so his family went to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They said: O Prophet of God, block so-and-so, for he is buying and there is a weakness in his knot. So the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, summoned him. So he forbade him from selling, saying: O Prophet of God, I am not patient with selling. He said: “If you are not abandoning the transaction, then say it and do not break it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7061 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7062","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith, Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Bilamani said: I saw an old man in Alexandria who was called Sarq. So I came to him and asked him, and he said to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named me and did not I would never let that go, so I said: Why did he name you? He said: A man from the desert came with two camels, so I bought them from him, then I entered my house and left behind, sold them and fulfilled my needs with them. I was absent until I thought that the Iraqi had left, but then the Iraqi was staying, so he took me and took me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. The news and he said: “What made you do what you did?” I said: I have fulfilled what I needed with their price, O Messenger of God. He said: “Fulfill it.” I said: I do not have it. He said: “You have stolen. Go, Iraqi, and sell it until you get your rights.” He said: So the people started calling him “I” and he turned to them and said: “What?” Do you want? They say: We want to ransom him from you. He said: By God, I am more deserving of you and have more need of God Almighty. Go, for I have freed you. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and did not He brings him out.”"
"7063","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Zahid and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us in Mecca, saying: Ishaq told us Ibn Ibrahim, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Muammar informed, on the authority of Bahz ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “And he imprisoned a man on a charge” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not release it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7063 - True"
"7064","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ammar bin Harun told me, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me Al-Adl, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Khuthaym told us, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imprisoned a man on charges for a day and a night as a precaution.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7064 - Ibrahim bin Khathim is abandoned"
"7065","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Wabr bin Abi Delilah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Maimunah, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who is present is mine, his honor is permissible.” And his punishment: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7065 - True"
"7066","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Al-Qanabi told us, and Ahmad bin Yunus told us, they said: Ibn Yunus told us: Abu Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both. He said: “The Messenger of God was cursed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the one who gives the briber and the one who takes the bribe.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the well-known hadith on the authority of Abu Hurairah and the hadith two dresses
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7066 - True"
"7067","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the briber and the bribe taker” in the ruling.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7067 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7068","So Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan al-Khazzaz told us, in Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Saeed Al-Asbahani, Yahya Ibn Abi Zakaria Ibn Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abi Zur’ah, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “May God curse the one who bribes, the one who takes a bribe, and the one who takes a bribe, and the one who takes a bribe, and the one who takes a bribe, and he who walks between them.” I only mentioned Omar bin Abi Salamah. Laith bin Abi Sulaym is based on the evidence, not the principles.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7068 - Omar and Laith were mentioned in the evidence"
"7069","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz, in Kufa, informed us. Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr bin told us. Muslim, Sa’dan bin Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He was placed in charge of ten, and he judged between them according to what they liked or disliked. He will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hands shackled to his neck. If he judges according to what God has revealed He did not take bribes in his ruling, nor was he unjust. May God redeem him on the Day of Resurrection, on the Day when there will be no wrong but his own, even if he rules by other than what God Almighty has revealed. And he took bribes in his judgment and preferred to have his left hand drawn to his right and he was thrown into Hell, but its bottom did not reach five hundred years.” Sa’dan bin Al-Walid Al-Bajli is a Kufi with few hadiths, and they did not narrate from him.”"
"7070","Ahmed bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Marhum bin Abdul Aziz Al-Attar told us, Sahl bin Attiya narrated to us, saying: I was with Bilal bin Abi Burdah in Al-Taff, and the man came and complained to him that the people of Al-Taff did not pay zakat. So Bilal sent a man to ask about what they were saying, and he found the man impugning his lineage, so he returned to Bilal and told him, so Bilal said “Allahu Akbar” and said: “Tell me.” My father, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever strives with people is without sound judgment, and there is some of that in him.” This is a hadith on the authority of Bilal bin Abi Burdah, and it has chains of narration. This is the most similar of them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7070 - What was authenticated and not authenticated"
"7071","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, Muhammad bin Ayyub informed us, Ghassan bin Malik informed us, Anbasa bin Abdul Rahman told us, about Alaq bin Abi Muslim, who said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is satisfied “Sultan by the wrath of his Lord, the Almighty, the Majestic, he departed from the religion of God, Blessed and Most High.” Allaq ibn Abi Muslim was the only one to mention it, and his narrators are all trustworthy. “The Last Book of Ahkam”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7071 - ‘Alaq was the only one to narrate it, and the narrators to him are trustworthy."
